# W44-119 chain-disable A/B — paired comparison
#
# Hypothesis tested: now that W44-117 (5604fdf0) ships an EPF
# sharpness seed for the buttloop's internal recon and W44-118
# (f543288c) gates that seed on `is_screenshot`, can the
# W44-105/107/108/109 qac-scale chain be retired (or reduced)
# without regressing the cells it currently improves?
#
# Mode A: chain ON  (current main, post-W44-118)
# Mode B: chain OFF (sets JXL_BUTTLOOP_INITIAL_QF_SCALE=1.0 AND
#                    JXL_W44_109_ADAPTIVE_QUANT_QF_SCALE=1.0)
#
# Both env knobs are read per-encode in butteraugli_loop.rs:
#   line 785: buttloop seed-scale (W44-105 + W44-107 + W44-108)
#   line 388: adaptive-quant pre-scale (W44-109)
# Setting both to 1.0 collapses the chain to a no-op.
#
# W44-117 EPF sharpness seed remains ACTIVE in both modes
# (independent of the chain — the seed is the buttloop's apply_epf
# input; the chain is the buttloop's initial quant_field).
#
# Cells (83 total):
#   terminal e5..=e9 × d ∈ {2, 3, 4, 5, 6}     (25 cells, canary)
#   codec_wiki e5..=e7 × d ∈ {3, 4, 5}         (9 cells, mid-d)
#   imac_g3 e5..=e9 × d ∈ {2, 3, 4}            (15 cells, mixed)
#   1025469 e7..=e9 × d ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4}         (8 cells, photo canary)
#   1418519 e7..=e9 × d ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4}         (8 cells, photo)
#   1189261 e7..=e9 × d ∈ {2, 3, 4}            (6 cells, photo)
#   1420710 e7..=e9 × d ∈ {2, 3, 4}            (6 cells, photo)
#   1531677 e7..=e9 × d ∈ {2, 3, 4}            (6 cells, photo)
#
# Interleaved (A, B, A, B, ...) per cell to reduce thermal/turbo
# bias across the long bench run.
#
git_rev: f543288ca1537381336736572f0ac6dff6396780 (W44-118 main)
host: lilith
cjxl_version: n/a (no cjxl baseline in this bench — pure jxl-encoder A/B)
decoder: jxl-oxide (request_color_encoding=srgb_linear)
metrics: butteraugli_linear (default params), fast_ssim2 (sRGB u8 from linear)
reproducer: cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' --example w44_119_chain_disable_ab > benchmarks/w44_119_chain_disable_ab_2026-05-20.tsv
#
# TSV schema:
#   image | effort | distance
#   | A_bytes | B_bytes | bytes_delta_pct (B vs A; + = B bigger)
#   | A_bfly  | B_bfly  | bfly_delta_pct  (B vs A; - = B better)
#   | A_ssim2 | B_ssim2 | ssim2_delta_abs (B vs A; + = B better)
#
# Headlines:
#   - 79 cells with data (4 OOM failures on imac_g3 e8/e9 high d,
#     same pre-existing budget cluster as the ledger sweep).
#   - Total bytes: 6,896,898 (A) → 5,466,435 (B) = -20.74% (chain
#     OFF saves bytes).
#   - Avg SSIM2 delta (B-A): -2.04 (chain OFF degrades quality).
#   - Avg butteraugli delta (B-A): +24.69% (chain OFF much worse).
#   - 42 cells with SSIM2 regression > 0.3 (chain-OFF loses).
#   - ZERO cells where chain OFF wins by > 0.3 SSIM2.
#
# Per-cluster averages (ssim2 delta B-A, bytes delta):
#   terminal   (n=25): ssim2 -3.86, bytes -25.71%
#   codec_wiki (n=9):  ssim2 -2.33, bytes -18.50%
#   imac_g3    (n=11): ssim2 -3.97, bytes -23.99%
#   photo      (n=34): ssim2 +0.00, bytes +0.00% (BYTE-IDENTICAL)
#
# Photos byte-identical confirms the chain's `is_screenshot` gate
# correctly skips photos regardless of env knob value.
#
# Worst per-cell screenshot regressions (B-A):
#   terminal e8 d=6: ssim2 -5.58
#   terminal e9 d=6: ssim2 -5.58
#   terminal e8 d=4: ssim2 -5.45
#   terminal e9 d=4: ssim2 -5.45
#   terminal e5 d=5: ssim2 -4.46
#   terminal e7 d=3: ssim2 -4.25
#   terminal e5 d=5: ssim2 -4.46
#
# Verdict: the chain CANNOT be retired. The W44-117/118 EPF seed
# fix addresses an ORTHOGONAL mechanism (buttloop-recon-vs-decoder
# delta) than the chain (buttloop-measurement bias). Disabling the
# chain regresses every screenshot cell.
#
# W44-120 plan:
#   1. KEEP the chain at its W44-109 magnitude (do not retire/reduce).
#   2. Investigate the terminal e8/e9 d=0.8 W44-117 over-correction
#      (-1.87 SSIM2 vs W44-110 baseline) surfaced by the ledger
#      refresh, as a distance-gate refinement on the W44-117 EPF
#      seed (probably gate at d >= 1.0).
